    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (66.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (65.47) lead our offensive charge as the premier starts. **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority play despite facing a southpaw in Prielipp; his elite sprint speed profile provides a floor that renders platoon concerns secondary in our SB-starved build. Meanwhile, **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park boost, elevating his efficiency score as he slots into the clean-up spot against Soriano. We are also leaning heavily on **Brice Turang** (62.96) and **Travis Bazzana** (61.45), both of whom capitalize on top-three batting order positioning to maximize their opportunities to contribute across the 5x5 categories.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young** (40.23), who hovered near the threshold of our starting lineup. While his plate discipline usually provides a high floor, he was edged out by **Kyle Karros** and **Alex Freeland**, as the optimizer favored their specific park factors and situational usage today. We are monitoring **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland** closely, as both rely on \"Lineup Pending\" projections against Gibson; should their actual batting orders drop further down the lineup than assumed, their scores\u2014already hampered by the #8/#9 slot penalties\u2014could slide further. Additionally, **Austin Riley** (44.97) faces a stern test against Misiorowski\u2019s 2.70 xERA; while he remains in the lineup for stability, he represents our highest risk of stagnation today. We continue to manage our depth with **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Trevor Story** sidelined, keeping a close eye on the health of our core as we preserve game caps for higher-leverage matchups.",
